  "overview": "The City of Los Altos uses Automated License Plate Reader (ALPR) technology to enhance public safety, improve investigative efficiency and support crime prevention efforts. ALPR cameras capture images of vehicle license plates and compare them against databases of stolen or wanted vehicles. This technology helps officers respond more quickly, identify suspects, recover stolen vehicles and locate missing persons. The Los Altos Police Department uses Flock Safety technology to capture objective evidence without compromising on individual privacy. Officers and detectives utilize retroactive searches to solve crimes after they've occurred. Additionally, Los Altos Police Department utilizes real time alerting of hotlist vehicles to capture wanted criminals. In an effort to ensure proper usage and make sure guardrails are in place, the department made the below policies and usage statistics available to the public.\n\nCommunity Impact\nData & Usage Summary",
